+ * whole sequence survives a watchdog or panic reset if the DRAM keeps its contents. Header (16
+ * bytes used of 64): magic 'OAKR', last sequence number, boot count, entry count; then 16-byte
+ * entries: mark, meta (cpu << 28 | in_interrupt << 27 | sequence & 0x7ffffff), CNTVCT low, high.
+ * The ring is never cleared: each boot continues the sequence, so the previous boot's tail is
+ * still there after the reset (read it with an mmap of /dev/mem; oakMOSS scripts/kmark-ring.py). */
+#include <asm/arch_timer.h>
